# REQUIRES: cargo
# The pinned real fill (evaluation/upstream/plonky3-replay/README.md;
# docs/spec/endpoints.md §6.4): the
# value-faithful FRI artifact's derived prover skeleton, filled in-process by
# the pinned crates through the backend runner, is checked along two bounded
# legs. The pinned PCS verifier accepts the runner's opening proof, and zkc's
# executor under the real profile accepts the assembled spine wire with an
# independently derived, entry-for-entry equal challenge stream. The runner
# recomputes the artifact identity before reading semantics, checks
# every recorded challenger event against the artifact's schedule under
# the declared correspondence relation (zero-bit commit pows enumerated,
# never silently matched), and a wrong fill is rejected by the pinned PCS
# verifier — the corrupted final polynomial shifts the transcript and
# the proof-of-work witness stops binding.
#
# Evidence boundaries of this record: the sealed source and its projections are
# zkc's; the fills and upstream acceptance are the pinned crates'; the runner's
# wire assembly is the named adapter; the witness codeword is the runner's own
# fixed input; universal conformance is not claimed by any of it.

# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: zkc-family %S/Inputs/plonky3-fri-vf.json --emit-vocabulary=%t/vocab.json --emit-spine=%t/spine.mlir
# RUN: zkc-opt '-pir-seal=protocol-vocabulary=%t/vocab.json construction-profile-registry=%zkc-registry-dir/construction-profiles.json' %t/spine.mlir -o %t/sealed.mlir
# RUN: zkc-opt '-pir-project=protocol-vocabulary=%t/vocab.json construction-profile-registry=%zkc-registry-dir/construction-profiles.json' %t/sealed.mlir -o %t/verifier.mlir
# RUN: zkc-opt '-pir-project=endpoint-kind=prover_skeleton protocol-vocabulary=%t/vocab.json construction-profile-registry=%zkc-registry-dir/construction-profiles.json' %t/sealed.mlir -o %t/prover.mlir
# RUN: zkc-translate --oir-canonical %t/prover.mlir -o %t/prover.json
# RUN: zkc-translate --oir-id %t/prover.mlir -o %t/prover.id
# RUN: zkc-translate --oir-id %t/verifier.mlir -o %t/verifier.id

# The runner: identity recomputed across languages, correspondence
# checked, wire assembled, upstream acceptance.
# RUN: cargo run --locked --quiet --manifest-path %zkc-replay-manifest --bin prove -- %t/prover.json > %t/runner.out
# RUN: FileCheck %s < %t/runner.out
# CHECK: artifact id: [[ID:[0-9a-f]{64}]]
# CHECK: correspondence: 19 artifact events matched 44 recorded challenger events (3 zero-bit commit pows enumerated as no-ops)
# CHECK: upstream verify: accepted the runner's proof at the pinned revision

# The recomputed identity equals the carrier's minted identity.
# RUN: grep "artifact id:" %t/runner.out | sed 's/artifact id: //' > %t/runner.id
# RUN: diff %t/runner.id %t/prover.id

# Leg 3a: zkc's executor accepts the runner's wire under the real
# profile and derives the same challenge stream.
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/build-runner-vectors.py %t/runner.out %t/verifier.id %t/vectors.json accept
# RUN: zkc-run %t/verifier.mlir --profile plonky3 --vectors %t/vectors.json | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=EXEC
# EXEC: runner-round-trip: accept

# A corrupted wire dies at the executor's grinding check — a verdict,
# never a refusal.
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/build-runner-vectors.py %t/runner.out %t/verifier.id %t/corrupt.json corrupt-nonce
# RUN: not zkc-run %t/verifier.mlir --profile plonky3 --vectors %t/corrupt.json | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CORRUPT
# CORRUPT: corrupted-nonce: check_failure

# A flipped byte inside an input authentication path dies at the
# native Merkle multi-opening check — the same verdict class, the
# query phase's own gate.
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/build-runner-vectors.py %t/runner.out %t/verifier.id %t/corrupt-path.json corrupt-path
# RUN: not zkc-run %t/verifier.mlir --profile plonky3 --vectors %t/corrupt-path.json | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CORRUPTPATH
# CORRUPTPATH: corrupted-path: check_failure

# A wrong fill is rejected by the pinned PCS verifier.
# RUN: cargo run --locked --quiet --manifest-path %zkc-replay-manifest --bin prove -- %t/prover.json corrupt-final-poly > %t/corrupt.out || true
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WRONGFILL < %t/corrupt.out
# WRONGFILL: upstream verify: rejected
